## Communications
## Metal–Organic Frameworks
Hosting ionic guests: An ionic liquid (IL) was incorporated within the micropores of a metal–organic framework (MOF). The phase behavior of the IL inside the MOF micropores was studied by differential scanning calorimetry and solidstate NMR measurements. The IL inside the micropores demonstrated no marked freezing transition down to low temperature, where the bulk IL was frozen.
